message:
style(trace): apply clang-format 14 to the izanagi trace changes

Run clang-format 14 (the major version used by
.github/workflows/format.yml) on the three files that the izanagi trace
instrumentation left unformatted: cc/mocc/transaction.cc,
cc/silo/transaction.cc and include/trace.hh. With this commit the
format job's check

  git ls-files -- cc include common | grep -E '\.(cc|hh|cpp)$' \
    | xargs clang-format --dry-run --Werror

passes on all 213 files.

Every reformatted line is inside an #if TRACE block. Where reformatting
changed the line count of a TRACE block, one #line directive after its
#endif restores the logical line numbers that the following code had in
the previous commit (cc/mocc/transaction.cc: #line 115;
cc/silo/transaction.cc: #line 365 and #line 381). Without them the
TRACE=0 build would change: ERR in cc/mocc/transaction.cc expands to
__LINE__ via NNN in include/debug.hh. With them every TRACE=0 source
line keeps its line number, so the TRACE=0 build is unchanged. No
tokens, string literals, comments or existing directives are changed.

